1.3.1 Perform a port scan - {Findings: Host is up (0.23s latency), Scanned in 77.79 seconds.}  
       1.3.2 Determine the services and versions on each open port - {Findings: 22/tcp: Open, SSH, OpenSSH 8.9p1 Ubuntu 3ubuntu0.10 (Ubuntu Linux; protocol 2.0); 81/tcp: Open, HTTP, Apache httpd (PHP 7.4.33), Robots.txt: 1 disallowed entry, HTTP Title: Login @ 12.0.3, HTTP Server Header: Apache.}  
       1.3.3 Enumerate HTTP Service on Port 81 - {Findings: Page Type: Login Window, Framework/Software: Dolibarr 12.0.3}  
       1.3.4 Vulnerability Analysis on Dolibarr 12.0.3 - {Findings: Vulnerability Identifier: CVE-2020-35136, Type: Authenticated Remote Code Execution (RCE), Date Identified: December 23, 2020, Description: The vulnerability arises from improper neutralization of special elements in commands within the backup function of Dolibarr 12.0.3. An authenticated attacker with access to the administrator dashboard can exploit this by manipulating the `zipfilename_template` parameter in `admin/tools/dolibarr_export.php`. Impact: Successful exploitation can lead to complete system compromise, allowing arbitrary code execution with web server privileges. CVSS Scores: CVSS v3.1 Base Score: 7.2 (HIGH), CVSS v2.0 Base Score: 9.0 (HIGH). Technical Details: The issue is due to a lack of proper sanitization of the `zipfilename_template` parameter, enabling command injection through crafted filenames. Mitigation and Remediation: A patch has been released that restricts the use of the `--` string in filenames. Organizations using Dolibarr 12.0.3 are strongly advised to upgrade to a patched version. Fix implemented via commit: `4fcd3fe49332baab0e424225ad10b76b47ebcbac`. Further References: NVD - CVE-2020-35136: [NVD Link](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-35136), GitHub Advisory: [GitHub Link](https://github.com/doli/dolibarr/security/advisories/GHSA-7gq7-hjgr-83g9), Wiz Blog on CVE-2020-35136: [Wiz Link](https://www.wiz.io/blog/cve-2020-35136-impact-exploitability-and-mitigation-steps), Exploit-DB Entry: [Exploit-DB Link](https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/49269).}  
       1.3.5 Exploit the selected exploitations - {Findings: Exploitation Status: Successful, Admin Login Information: Username Found: admin, Time to Guess Admin Login: 546.76 seconds, Admin Password Information: Crypted Password Found: 5fec4ba8376f..., Time to Guess Admin Password (Crypted): 1520.36 seconds, Full Crypted Password: 5fec4ba8376f207d1ff2f0cac0882b01, Overall Exploit Duration: 2550.05 seconds, Credentials Obtained: Username: admin, Crypted Password: 5fec4ba8376f207d1ff2f0cac0882b01. This summary provides key findings from the successful exploitation, including the admin username and the crypted password, which are critical for further analysis and potential access escalation.}  
   1.4 Crack the password hash - {Findings: Hash Status: Successfully Cracked, Cracked Password: admin!@#. This summary indicates that the hash has been successfully cracked, revealing the password "admin!@#," which may be pertinent for further penetration testing activities or access attempts.}  
